        <item>
            <title>0.1.7-beta</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 17:14:33 +0200</pubDate>
            <link>https://typoless.app</link>
            <sparkle:channel>beta</sparkle:channel>
            <sparkle:version>108</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.1.7-beta</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Corrections</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Apple's on-device model turns ordinary text down now and again, and when it did, Typoless corrected nothing and said nothing about it. It now asks a second time in a wording the model accepts, which gets the correction you expected.</li>
    <li>Where even the second attempt is turned down, the text is left alone and the history says so, rather than reporting that there was nothing to fix.</li>
</ul>
<h3>History</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Every pass now has a reason for each piece of text it left alone, including the ones the model would not read.</li>
    <li>A line the model returned exactly as you wrote it is no longer reported as a translation.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
